                            <comment id="503418" author="paf0186" created="Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:50:53 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The &quot;Expect 3 found on mds1&quot; duplicate OST scan is fixed by &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/68698&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/68698&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17891&quot; title=&quot;sanity-lfsck test_18e: Expect 2 orphans have been fixed, but got: 4&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-17891&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-17891&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;), landed 2026-09-29. Every failure since then that we checked tested a base without it. Disabling 68698&apos;s two queue guards reproduces the failure locally; with them, 10/10 controlled runs passed. Failures on older bases go away after a rebase.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A separate signature (an object left over from test_18a) is seen only on 68928 and is not covered here.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
